  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202x} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(3x+y)\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\sqrt{x+y})}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(x+y))}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot 1)}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)-(3x+y)}{2\\sqrt{x+y}})}{x+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+5y}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=3x+5y.\n$$",
